3. Mini Project — Bulk Opportunity Processor | ~25 min

Today extend yesterday's project.

Requirement

When Opportunities transition to Closed Won:

Update related Account Customer_Status__c = 'Active'

Must support 200 Opportunities

Multiple Opportunities may share one Account

Do not update the same Account repeatedly

Include proper tests


Build:

OpportunityTrigger
        ↓
OpportunityTriggerHandler
        ↓
OpportunityService
        ↓
Account update

Trigger

Your trigger should be tiny:

trigger OpportunityTrigger
on Opportunity (after update) {

    OpportunityTriggerHandler.afterUpdate(
        Trigger.new,
        Trigger.oldMap
    );
}

Handler responsibility

Detect:

old Stage != Closed Won
AND
new Stage == Closed Won

Collect:

Set<Id> accountIds

Then call:

OpportunityService.activateAccounts(accountIds);

Service responsibility

Create/update Accounts in bulk.

No DML inside loops.

Test requirements

Create:

2 Accounts
↓
200 Opportunities
↓
100 belong to Account A
100 belong to Account B
↓
update all to Closed Won

Then assert:

Account A → Active
Account B → Active

Also add a negative scenario:

Opportunity:
Prospecting → Negotiation

Expected:

Account status must NOT change

This is already much closer to the type of code discussion you may get in a Salesforce Developer interview.


