4. Git/GitHub + Harness/CI/CD | ~10 min

Scenario:

You created:

feature/SF-1023

Another developer changed the same class on main.

Before PR you do:

git checkout main
git pull origin main

git checkout feature/SF-1023
git merge main

Conflict:

<<<<<<< HEAD
your change
=======
main branch change
>>>>>>> main

You manually decide the correct final code, remove conflict markers, then:

git add .
git commit

Don't say in an interview:

> “Git automatically chooses whichever code is latest.”



A merge conflict requires understanding both intended changes.

CI/CD mental model

For Salesforce:

Developer
   ↓
Git feature branch
   ↓
Pull Request
   ↓
Validation pipeline
   ↓
Apex tests / quality checks
   ↓
Approval
   ↓
Merge
   ↓
Deployment pipeline
   ↓
Target Salesforce environment

A platform such as Harness can orchestrate deployment pipelines, approvals and related software-delivery controls.

Since Harness is on your actual experience path, eventually you should be able to explain what happened from Git commit → validation → deployment, rather than only saying “I worked on Harness.”


